※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4512

※ `⎕typeof` takes something lifted and nothing else.  A type's name and a
※ value's name are both identifiers, and a type written out in full is not an
※ expression at all, so what follows it cannot be read without knowing what the
※ names turned out to mean -- which is the thing the brackets are there to
※ stop.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = 1u8
    comptime if ⎕typeof(n) = ⌜u8⌝:
        0u6
    else:
        1u6
